# Test-run artifacts. The harness (test-lib.sh) executes each script inside a
# per-PID `trash.<pid>` working directory, and some stress tests build repos
# directly in their CWD. None of this should ever be committed — in particular
# `extreme-path-test` builds a 20-level-deep directory tree that exceeds the
# Windows MAX_PATH limit and breaks `git checkout` on Windows CI runners.
trash.*/
test-results/
extreme-path-test/
